                <pb facs="1590" n="1432" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1432"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Russell to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.—Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Russell reports that he has advised the Venezuelan Government that France
                    has severed diplomatic relations with it, and that after the departure of the
                    French chargé d’affaires he will take charge of the French interests and
                    archives. He says he thinks it is advisable for the chargé d’affaires to leave
                    at once, and as no steamer leaves immediately, a naval vessel should be sent for
                    him.)</p>
            </div>
